group Sub
SubShape    "Sub shape"     0 3    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw Square   | Sub oscillator wave
    how Chooses the wave of the sub oscillator: sine, triangle, saw or square.
    sound Sine is clean and deep, square is hollow and strong, saw is bright and buzzy.
SubOct      "Sub octave"    0 2    1    enum 0 -1 -2                    | Octaves from the note
    how Sets how many octaves below the note the sub sounds: 0, 1 or 2.
    sound Lower adds weight and rumble under the main sound.
SubLevel    "Sub level"     0 1000 0    pct                             | Sub level
    how Sets the level of the sub oscillator, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound It adds deep body to basses and thickness under leads; too much eats headroom.
SubPan      "Sub pan"       0 1000 500  bip                             | Sub pan
    how Places the sub oscillator in the stereo field, from left to right.
    sound Keep it in the middle so the low end stays focused.
SubToF2     "Sub → filter 2" 0 1000 0   pct                             | Balance between filter 1 (0 %) and filter 2 (100 %)
    how Balances the sub between the first filter (0 %) and the second (100 %).
    sound It decides which filter shapes the sub.

group Noise
NoiseColor  "Noise color"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | 0 %: dark (lowpassed from 100 Hz); 100 %: white
    how Sets the colour of the noise, from dark (0 %, low-passed from 100 Hz) to white (100 %).
    sound Dark noise sounds like a soft rumble or wind; white noise sounds hissy and bright.
NoiseLevel  "Noise level"   0 1000 0    pct                             | Noise level
    how Sets the level of the noise source, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A little adds breath and air; a lot gives hiss, wind and percussive snap.
NoisePan    "Noise pan"     0 1000 500  bip                             | Noise pan
    how Places the noise in the stereo field, from left to right.
    sound Off-centre noise makes the sound feel wider.
NoiseToF2   "Noise → filter 2" 0 1000 0 pct                             | Balance between filter 1 (0 %) and filter 2 (100 %)
    how Balances the noise between the first filter (0 %) and the second (100 %).
    sound It decides which filter shapes the noise.

group Filter 1
F1Type      "F1 type"       0 12   1    enum Off Ladder_24 Ladder_12 LP_12 LP_24 BP_12 BP_24 HP_12 HP_24 Notch Peak Comb+ Comb− | Filter model (Comb: the cutoff is its pitch)
    how Chooses the model of filter 1: off, ladder, low-pass, band-pass, high-pass, notch, peak or comb.
    sound Ladders sound warm and thick, the others clean or specialised, and combs ring at the pitch of the cutoff.
F1Cutoff    "F1 cutoff"     0 1000 750  freq 20 20000                   | Cutoff
    how Sets the cutoff frequency of filter 1, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz (for a comb, its pitch).
    sound Lower sounds darker and duller; higher sounds brighter and more open.
F1Reso      "F1 reso"       0 1000 150  pct                             | Resonance (comb: feedback)
    how Sets the resonance of filter 1 (for a comb, its feedback), from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More resonance adds a whistling peak at the cutoff; a comb near 100 % rings loudly.
F1Drive     "F1 drive"      0 1000 0    lin 0 24 dB 1                   | Drive into the filter
    how Pushes the signal harder into filter 1, from 0 to 24 dB.
    sound More drive adds warmth and grit; too much distorts and gets loud.
F1Env       "F1 env"        0 1000 600  lin -6 6 oct 1                  | Filter envelope amount
    how Sets how far the filter envelope moves the cutoff of filter 1, from -6 to +6 octaves.
    sound Positive opens the filter with each note for a plucky sweep; negative closes it.
F1Key       "F1 key track"  0 1000 500  pct                             | Cutoff follows the keyboard (100 %: an octave per octave)
    how Sets how much the cutoff of filter 1 follows the keyboard, from 0 to 100 % (100 % is an octave per octave).
    sound At 100 % the tone stays the same brightness across the keyboard; at 0 % high notes sound duller.
F1Vel       "F1 vel"        0 1000 250  lin 0 4 oct 1                   | Softer notes close the filter by up to this
    how Sets how much softer notes close filter 1, by up to 4 octaves.
    sound Soft playing sounds darker and hard playing brighter.

group Filter 2
F2Type      "F2 type"       0 12   0    enum Off Ladder_24 Ladder_12 LP_12 LP_24 BP_12 BP_24 HP_12 HP_24 Notch Peak Comb+ Comb− | Filter model (Comb: the cutoff is its pitch)
    how Chooses the model of filter 2: off, ladder, low-pass, band-pass, high-pass, notch, peak or comb.
    sound Ladders sound warm and thick, the others clean or specialised, and combs ring at the pitch of the cutoff.
F2Cutoff    "F2 cutoff"     0 1000 750  freq 20 20000                   | Cutoff
    how Sets the cutoff frequency of filter 2, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz (for a comb, its pitch).
    sound Lower sounds darker and duller; higher sounds brighter and more open.
F2Reso      "F2 reso"       0 1000 150  pct                             | Resonance (comb: feedback)
    how Sets the resonance of filter 2 (for a comb, its feedback), from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More resonance adds a whistling peak at the cutoff; a comb near 100 % rings loudly.
F2Drive     "F2 drive"      0 1000 0    lin 0 24 dB 1                   | Drive into the filter
    how Pushes the signal harder into filter 2, from 0 to 24 dB.
    sound More drive adds warmth and grit; too much distorts and gets loud.
F2Env       "F2 env"        0 1000 500  lin -6 6 oct 1                  | Filter envelope amount
    how Sets how far the filter envelope moves the cutoff of filter 2, from -6 to +6 octaves.
    sound Positive opens the filter with each note for a plucky sweep; negative closes it.
F2Key       "F2 key track"  0 1000 500  pct                             | Cutoff follows the keyboard (100 %: an octave per octave)
    how Sets how much the cutoff of filter 2 follows the keyboard, from 0 to 100 % (100 % is an octave per octave).
    sound At 100 % the tone stays the same brightness across the keyboard; at 0 % high notes sound duller.
F2Vel       "F2 vel"        0 1000 0  lin 0 4 oct 1                   | Softer notes close the filter by up to this
    how Sets how much softer notes close filter 2, by up to 4 octaves.
    sound Soft playing sounds darker and hard playing brighter.
Routing     "Filter routing" 0 1000 0   pct                             | 0 %: filter 1 into filter 2 (serial); 100 %: side by side (parallel)
    how Sets how the two filters connect, from in series (0 %) to side by side (100 %).
    sound Series cuts more and sounds stronger; parallel blends two different filter tones.

group Amp env
AmpA        "Amp attack"    0 1000 100  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
    how Sets how long the amplitude envelope takes to rise, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Short is a sharp, immediate start; long fades the note in like a pad.
AmpD        "Amp decay"     0 1000 500  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
    how Sets how long the amplitude envelope takes to fall to the sustain level, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Short with low sustain gives plucks and stabs; long keeps the note open.
AmpS        "Amp sustain"   0 1000 800  pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the level the amplitude envelope holds while a key is down, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound 100 % holds full volume like an organ; 0 % makes every note decay like a pluck.
AmpR        "Amp release"   0 1000 450  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
    how Sets how long the sound takes to fade after the key is released, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Short stops the note at once; long lets it ring out like a pad tail.

group Filter env
FltA        "Flt attack"    0 1000 100  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to rise, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Long makes the sound open up slowly; short gives an instant bright attack.
FltD        "Flt decay"     0 1000 520  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to fall to its sustain, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Short sounds plucky and snappy; long keeps the filter movement slow.
FltS        "Flt sustain"   0 1000 300  pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the level the filter envelope holds while a key is down, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher keeps the filter open and the tone bright during the note.
FltR        "Flt release"   0 1000 450  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to close after the key is released, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Longer makes the tail go on darkening after the note ends.

# P1b (appended): the Analog engine's parameters for each slot.
group Osc A
AShape     "A shape"       0 4    2    enum Sine Triangle Saw Square Pulse | The Analog engine's wave
    how Chooses the wave of slot A's Analog engine: sine, triangle, saw, square or pulse.
    sound Sine is pure, triangle soft, saw bright and buzzy, square hollow and woody, and pulse thin and nasal.
APw        "A pulse width" 0 1000 1000 lin 3 50 % 1                   | The Analog engine's pulse width (Pulse)
    how Sets the pulse width of slot A's Analog engine when the shape is Pulse, from 3 to 50 %.
    sound 50 % is a hollow square; narrower pulses sound thinner and more nasal.
ADrift     "A drift"       0 1000 200  pct                             | The Analog engine's voices each a little out of tune (up to ±12 cents), as analog oscillators are
    how Lets each voice of slot A's Analog engine wander a little out of tune, by up to 12 cents.
    sound It adds the slow, imperfect movement of analog oscillators and makes stacks feel alive.
group Osc B
BShape     "B shape"       0 4    2    enum Sine Triangle Saw Square Pulse | The Analog engine's wave
    how Chooses the wave of slot B's Analog engine: sine, triangle, saw, square or pulse.
    sound Sine is pure, triangle soft, saw bright and buzzy, square hollow and woody, and pulse thin and nasal.
BPw        "B pulse width" 0 1000 1000 lin 3 50 % 1                   | The Analog engine's pulse width (Pulse)
    how Sets the pulse width of slot B's Analog engine when the shape is Pulse, from 3 to 50 %.
    sound 50 % is a hollow square; narrower pulses sound thinner and more nasal.
BDrift     "B drift"       0 1000 200  pct                             | The Analog engine's voices each a little out of tune (up to ±12 cents), as analog oscillators are
    how Lets each voice of slot B's Analog engine wander a little out of tune, by up to 12 cents.
    sound It adds the slow, imperfect movement of analog oscillators and makes stacks feel alive.
group Osc C
CShape     "C shape"       0 4    2    enum Sine Triangle Saw Square Pulse | The Analog engine's wave
    how Chooses the wave of slot C's Analog engine: sine, triangle, saw, square or pulse.
    sound Sine is pure, triangle soft, saw bright and buzzy, square hollow and woody, and pulse thin and nasal.
CPw        "C pulse width" 0 1000 1000 lin 3 50 % 1                   | The Analog engine's pulse width (Pulse)
    how Sets the pulse width of slot C's Analog engine when the shape is Pulse, from 3 to 50 %.
    sound 50 % is a hollow square; narrower pulses sound thinner and more nasal.
CDrift     "C drift"       0 1000 200  pct                             | The Analog engine's voices each a little out of tune (up to ±12 cents), as analog oscillators are
    how Lets each voice of slot C's Analog engine wander a little out of tune, by up to 12 cents.
    sound It adds the slow, imperfect movement of analog oscillators and makes stacks feel alive.

# P1b (appended): modulation. Two DAHDSR envelopes with curves, four LFOs, four macros and sixteen
# routes (source, destination, amount), evaluated per note on the control grid.
group Mod env 1
E1Delay    "Env1 delay"    0 1000 0    pow 0 10 3 s 3                  | Delay before the attack
    how Sets the delay before modulation envelope 1 starts, from 0 to 10 s.
    sound The modulation it drives begins late, so a vibrato or sweep comes in after the note starts.
E1A        "Env1 attack"   0 1000 300  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
    how Sets the attack time of modulation envelope 1, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Longer makes what it controls fade in slowly.
E1Hold     "Env1 hold"     0 1000 0    pow 0 10 3 s 3                  | Hold at the top
    how Sets how long modulation envelope 1 stays at the top before decaying, from 0 to 10 s.
    sound A hold keeps the modulation at full strength for a while before it falls.
E1D        "Env1 decay"    0 1000 600  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
    how Sets the decay time of modulation envelope 1, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Shorter makes a quick blip; longer a slow fall.
E1S        "Env1 sustain"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the sustain level of modulation envelope 1, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher keeps the modulation on while the key is held.
E1R        "Env1 release"  0 1000 500  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
    how Sets the release time of modulation envelope 1, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Longer makes the modulation fade out slowly after the key is released.
E1ACurve   "Env1 att curve" 0 1000 500 bip                             | Attack shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
    how Shapes the attack of modulation envelope 1, from fast start (-100 %) through straight (0) to slow start (+100 %).
    sound A fast start rises quickly and eases in; a slow start builds up late.
E1DCurve   "Env1 dec curve" 0 1000 200 bip                             | Decay shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
    how Shapes the decay of modulation envelope 1, from fast start (-100 %) through straight (0) to slow start (+100 %).
    sound A fast start drops quickly then lingers; a slow start holds then drops.
E1RCurve   "Env1 rel curve" 0 1000 200 bip                             | Release shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
    how Shapes the release of modulation envelope 1, from fast start (-100 %) through straight (0) to slow start (+100 %).
    sound A fast start drops quickly then lingers; a slow start holds then drops.
E1Sync     "Env1 sync"     0 1    0    switch Seconds Beats            | Beats: each time is read as beats of the song's tempo (1 s = 1 beat)
    how Chooses whether modulation envelope 1 times are read in seconds or in beats of the song tempo.
    sound Beats keep the envelope locked to the tempo; seconds stay fixed.
group Mod env 2
E2Delay    "Env2 delay"    0 1000 0    pow 0 10 3 s 3                  | Delay before the attack
    how Sets the delay before modulation envelope 2 starts, from 0 to 10 s.
    sound The modulation it drives begins late, so a vibrato or sweep comes in after the note starts.
E2A        "Env2 attack"   0 1000 300  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
    how Sets the attack time of modulation envelope 2, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Longer makes what it controls fade in slowly.
E2Hold     "Env2 hold"     0 1000 0    pow 0 10 3 s 3                  | Hold at the top
    how Sets how long modulation envelope 2 stays at the top before decaying, from 0 to 10 s.
    sound A hold keeps the modulation at full strength for a while before it falls.
E2D        "Env2 decay"    0 1000 600  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
    how Sets the decay time of modulation envelope 2, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Shorter makes a quick blip; longer a slow fall.
E2S        "Env2 sustain"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the sustain level of modulation envelope 2, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher keeps the modulation on while the key is held.
E2R        "Env2 release"  0 1000 500  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
    how Sets the release time of modulation envelope 2, from 0.5 ms to 20 s.
    sound Longer makes the modulation fade out slowly after the key is released.
E2ACurve   "Env2 att curve" 0 1000 500 bip                             | Attack shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
    how Shapes the attack of modulation envelope 2, from fast start (-100 %) through straight (0) to slow start (+100 %).
    sound A fast start rises quickly and eases in; a slow start builds up late.
E2DCurve   "Env2 dec curve" 0 1000 200 bip                             | Decay shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
    how Shapes the decay of modulation envelope 2, from fast start (-100 %) through straight (0) to slow start (+100 %).
    sound A fast start drops quickly then lingers; a slow start holds then drops.
E2RCurve   "Env2 rel curve" 0 1000 200 bip                             | Release shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
    how Shapes the release of modulation envelope 2, from fast start (-100 %) through straight (0) to slow start (+100 %).
    sound A fast start drops quickly then lingers; a slow start holds then drops.
E2Sync     "Env2 sync"     0 1    0    switch Seconds Beats            | Beats: each time is read as beats of the song's tempo (1 s = 1 beat)
    how Chooses whether modulation envelope 2 times are read in seconds or in beats of the song tempo.
    sound Beats keep the envelope locked to the tempo; seconds stay fixed.
group LFO 1
L1Shape    "LFO1 shape"    0 7    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth Drawn | Waveform (Drawn: the LFO's own breakpoints, drawn in the editor)
    how Chooses the wave of LFO 1: sine, triangle, saw up or down, square, sample and hold, smooth random, or your drawn shape.
    sound Sine is smooth, square jumps, sample and hold steps randomly, and a drawn shape follows your own curve.
L1Rate     "LFO1 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
    how Sets the speed of LFO 1 when it is free-running, from 0.02 to 50 Hz.
    sound Slow gives a gentle drift or sweep; fast gives vibrato, tremolo or buzz.
L1Sync     "LFO1 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
    how Locks LFO 1 to the song tempo with a note length from 1/32 to 4 bars, or leaves it free.
    sound A synced LFO stays in time with the music and overrides the rate.
L1Retrig   "LFO1 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (one per note); off: one free LFO for all notes
    how Chooses whether LFO 1 restarts with every note or runs freely for all notes.
    sound Restarting makes every note move the same way; free-running makes each note differ.
L1Phase    "LFO1 phase"    0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase (retrig)
    how Sets where LFO 1 starts in its cycle, from 0 to 360 degrees, when it restarts per note.
    sound It shifts where the movement begins on each note.
L1Fade     "LFO1 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
    how Sets how long LFO 1 takes to fade in after a note starts, from 0 to 5 s.
    sound A fade-in brings in vibrato or movement gradually instead of at once.
group LFO 2
L2Shape    "LFO2 shape"    0 7    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth Drawn | Waveform (Drawn: the LFO's own breakpoints, drawn in the editor)
    how Chooses the wave of LFO 2: sine, triangle, saw up or down, square, sample and hold, smooth random, or your drawn shape.
    sound Sine is smooth, square jumps, sample and hold steps randomly, and a drawn shape follows your own curve.
L2Rate     "LFO2 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
    how Sets the speed of LFO 2 when it is free-running, from 0.02 to 50 Hz.
    sound Slow gives a gentle drift or sweep; fast gives vibrato, tremolo or buzz.
L2Sync     "LFO2 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
    how Locks LFO 2 to the song tempo with a note length from 1/32 to 4 bars, or leaves it free.
    sound A synced LFO stays in time with the music and overrides the rate.
L2Retrig   "LFO2 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (one per note); off: one free LFO for all notes
    how Chooses whether LFO 2 restarts with every note or runs freely for all notes.
    sound Restarting makes every note move the same way; free-running makes each note differ.
L2Phase    "LFO2 phase"    0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase (retrig)
    how Sets where LFO 2 starts in its cycle, from 0 to 360 degrees, when it restarts per note.
    sound It shifts where the movement begins on each note.
L2Fade     "LFO2 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
    how Sets how long LFO 2 takes to fade in after a note starts, from 0 to 5 s.
    sound A fade-in brings in vibrato or movement gradually instead of at once.
group LFO 3
L3Shape    "LFO3 shape"    0 7    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth Drawn | Waveform (Drawn: the LFO's own breakpoints, drawn in the editor)
    how Chooses the wave of LFO 3: sine, triangle, saw up or down, square, sample and hold, smooth random, or your drawn shape.
    sound Sine is smooth, square jumps, sample and hold steps randomly, and a drawn shape follows your own curve.
L3Rate     "LFO3 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
    how Sets the speed of LFO 3 when it is free-running, from 0.02 to 50 Hz.
    sound Slow gives a gentle drift or sweep; fast gives vibrato, tremolo or buzz.
L3Sync     "LFO3 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
    how Locks LFO 3 to the song tempo with a note length from 1/32 to 4 bars, or leaves it free.
    sound A synced LFO stays in time with the music and overrides the rate.
L3Retrig   "LFO3 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (one per note); off: one free LFO for all notes
    how Chooses whether LFO 3 restarts with every note or runs freely for all notes.
    sound Restarting makes every note move the same way; free-running makes each note differ.
L3Phase    "LFO3 phase"    0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase (retrig)
    how Sets where LFO 3 starts in its cycle, from 0 to 360 degrees, when it restarts per note.
    sound It shifts where the movement begins on each note.
L3Fade     "LFO3 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
    how Sets how long LFO 3 takes to fade in after a note starts, from 0 to 5 s.
    sound A fade-in brings in vibrato or movement gradually instead of at once.
group LFO 4
L4Shape    "LFO4 shape"    0 7    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth Drawn | Waveform (Drawn: the LFO's own breakpoints, drawn in the editor)
    how Chooses the wave of LFO 4: sine, triangle, saw up or down, square, sample and hold, smooth random, or your drawn shape.
    sound Sine is smooth, square jumps, sample and hold steps randomly, and a drawn shape follows your own curve.
L4Rate     "LFO4 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
    how Sets the speed of LFO 4 when it is free-running, from 0.02 to 50 Hz.
    sound Slow gives a gentle drift or sweep; fast gives vibrato, tremolo or buzz.
L4Sync     "LFO4 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
    how Locks LFO 4 to the song tempo with a note length from 1/32 to 4 bars, or leaves it free.
    sound A synced LFO stays in time with the music and overrides the rate.
L4Retrig   "LFO4 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (one per note); off: one free LFO for all notes
    how Chooses whether LFO 4 restarts with every note or runs freely for all notes.
    sound Restarting makes every note move the same way; free-running makes each note differ.
L4Phase    "LFO4 phase"    0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase (retrig)
    how Sets where LFO 4 starts in its cycle, from 0 to 360 degrees, when it restarts per note.
    sound It shifts where the movement begins on each note.
L4Fade     "LFO4 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
    how Sets how long LFO 4 takes to fade in after a note starts, from 0 to 5 s.
    sound A fade-in brings in vibrato or movement gradually instead of at once.
group Macros
M1       "Macro 1"       0 1000 0    pct                             | A knob for routes to follow
    how Sets macro 1, a single knob that modulation routes can follow, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Routes make this one knob move several things at once; it does nothing alone.
M2       "Macro 2"       0 1000 0    pct                             | A knob for routes to follow
    how Sets macro 2, a single knob that modulation routes can follow, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Routes make this one knob move several things at once; it does nothing alone.
M3       "Macro 3"       0 1000 0    pct                             | A knob for routes to follow
    how Sets macro 3, a single knob that modulation routes can follow, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Routes make this one knob move several things at once; it does nothing alone.
M4       "Macro 4"       0 1000 0    pct                             | A knob for routes to follow
    how Sets macro 4, a single knob that modulation routes can follow, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Routes make this one knob move several things at once; it does nothing alone.
group Routes
R1Src      "R1 source"     0 22   0    enum Off Mod_env_1 Mod_env_2 LFO_1 LFO_2 LFO_3 LFO_4 Amp_env Filter_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Macro_1 Macro_2 Macro_3 Macro_4 Random MPE_pressure MPE_slide MPE_bend Seq_step Seq_velocity | Route 1: what modulates
    how Chooses what drives route 1: an envelope, LFO, velocity, key, wheel, aftertouch, macro, random, MPE or sequencer source.
    sound The source decides what moves the destination; Off turns the route off.
R1Dst      "R1 dest"       0 27   0    enum Off Pitch A_pitch B_pitch C_pitch A_position B_position C_position A_warp_1 A_warp_2 B_warp_1 B_warp_2 C_warp_1 C_warp_2 A_level B_level C_level Sub_level Noise_level F1_cutoff F2_cutoff F1_reso F2_reso Amp LFO_1_rate LFO_2_rate LFO_3_rate LFO_4_rate | Route 1: what it moves
    how Chooses what route 1 moves: pitch, a slot's position, warp or level, the sub or noise level, a filter cutoff or resonance, the amplitude or an LFO rate.
    sound The destination decides what changes with the source; Off turns the route off.
R1Amt      "R1 amount"     0 1000 500  bip                             | Route 1: how far (pitch ±12 st, cutoff ±6 oct, LFO rate ±4 oct, the rest their whole range)
    how Sets how far route 1 moves its destination, from -100 to +100 % (pitch 12 semitones, cutoff 6 octaves, LFO rate 4 octaves at full).
    sound Negative values move it the opposite way; 0 % does nothing.
R2Src      "R2 source"     0 22   0    enum Off Mod_env_1 Mod_env_2 LFO_1 LFO_2 LFO_3 LFO_4 Amp_env Filter_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Macro_1 Macro_2 Macro_3 Macro_4 Random MPE_pressure MPE_slide MPE_bend Seq_step Seq_velocity | Route 2: what modulates
    how Chooses what drives route 2: an envelope, LFO, velocity, key, wheel, aftertouch, macro, random, MPE or sequencer source.
    sound The source decides what moves the destination; Off turns the route off.
R2Dst      "R2 dest"       0 27   0    enum Off Pitch A_pitch B_pitch C_pitch A_position B_position C_position A_warp_1 A_warp_2 B_warp_1 B_warp_2 C_warp_1 C_warp_2 A_level B_level C_level Sub_level Noise_level F1_cutoff F2_cutoff F1_reso F2_reso Amp LFO_1_rate LFO_2_rate LFO_3_rate LFO_4_rate | Route 2: what it moves
    how Chooses what route 2 moves: pitch, a slot's position, warp or level, the sub or noise level, a filter cutoff or resonance, the amplitude or an LFO rate.
    sound The destination decides what changes with the source; Off turns the route off.
R2Amt      "R2 amount"     0 1000 500  bip                             | Route 2: how far (pitch ±12 st, cutoff ±6 oct, LFO rate ±4 oct, the rest their whole range)
    how Sets how far route 2 moves its destination, from -100 to +100 % (pitch 12 semitones, cutoff 6 octaves, LFO rate 4 octaves at full).
    sound Negative values move it the opposite way; 0 % does nothing.
R3Src      "R3 source"     0 22   0    enum Off Mod_env_1 Mod_env_2 LFO_1 LFO_2 LFO_3 LFO_4 Amp_env Filter_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Macro_1 Macro_2 Macro_3 Macro_4 Random MPE_pressure MPE_slide MPE_bend Seq_step Seq_velocity | Route 3: what modulates
    how Chooses what drives route 3: an envelope, LFO, velocity, key, wheel, aftertouch, macro, random, MPE or sequencer source.
    sound The source decides what moves the destination; Off turns the route off.
R3Dst      "R3 dest"       0 27   0    enum Off Pitch A_pitch B_pitch C_pitch A_position B_position C_position A_warp_1 A_warp_2 B_warp_1 B_warp_2 C_warp_1 C_warp_2 A_level B_level C_level Sub_level Noise_level F1_cutoff F2_cutoff F1_reso F2_reso Amp LFO_1_rate LFO_2_rate LFO_3_rate LFO_4_rate | Route 3: what it moves
    how Chooses what route 3 moves: pitch, a slot's position, warp or level, the sub or noise level, a filter cutoff or resonance, the amplitude or an LFO rate.
    sound The destination decides what changes with the source; Off turns the route off.
R3Amt      "R3 amount"     0 1000 500  bip                             | Route 3: how far (pitch ±12 st, cutoff ±6 oct, LFO rate ±4 oct, the rest their whole range)
    how Sets how far route 3 moves its destination, from -100 to +100 % (pitch 12 semitones, cutoff 6 octaves, LFO rate 4 octaves at full).
    sound Negative values move it the opposite way; 0 % does nothing.
R4Src      "R4 source"     0 22   0    enum Off Mod_env_1 Mod_env_2 LFO_1 LFO_2 LFO_3 LFO_4 Amp_env Filter_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Macro_1 Macro_2 Macro_3 Macro_4 Random MPE_pressure MPE_slide MPE_bend Seq_step Seq_velocity | Route 4: what modulates
    how Chooses what drives route 4: an envelope, LFO, velocity, key, wheel, aftertouch, macro, random, MPE or sequencer source.
    sound The source decides what moves the destination; Off turns the route off.
R4Dst      "R4 dest"       0 27   0    enum Off Pitch A_pitch B_pitch C_pitch A_position B_position C_position A_warp_1 A_warp_2 B_warp_1 B_warp_2 C_warp_1 C_warp_2 A_level B_level C_level Sub_level Noise_level F1_cutoff F2_cutoff F1_reso F2_reso Amp LFO_1_rate LFO_2_rate LFO_3_rate LFO_4_rate | Route 4: what it moves
    how Chooses what route 4 moves: pitch, a slot's position, warp or level, the sub or noise level, a filter cutoff or resonance, the amplitude or an LFO rate.
    sound The destination decides what changes with the source; Off turns the route off.
R4Amt      "R4 amount"     0 1000 500  bip                             | Route 4: how far (pitch ±12 st, cutoff ±6 oct, LFO rate ±4 oct, the rest their whole range)
    how Sets how far route 4 moves its destination, from -100 to +100 % (pitch 12 semitones, cutoff 6 octaves, LFO rate 4 octaves at full).
    sound Negative values move it the opposite way; 0 % does nothing.
R5Src      "R5 source"     0 22   0    enum Off Mod_env_1 Mod_env_2 LFO_1 LFO_2 LFO_3 LFO_4 Amp_env Filter_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Macro_1 Macro_2 Macro_3 Macro_4 Random MPE_pressure MPE_slide MPE_bend Seq_step Seq_velocity | Route 5: what modulates
    how Chooses what drives route 5: an envelope, LFO, velocity, key, wheel, aftertouch, macro, random, MPE or sequencer source.
    sound The source decides what moves the destination; Off turns the route off.
