# P2 (appended): the Sample and Granular engines' parameters for each slot. "position" (above) is the
# sample's start (Sample) or the centre grains are taken from (Granular); tuning, level, pan, unison,
# detune and spread are the slot's own. Samples and grains take no warps.
group Osc A
ASmpSrc    "A sample"      0 5    0    enum Choir Strings Bell Pluck Texture User | The sample the Sample and Granular engines play (built-in ones are made by code; User: one loaded for this slot)
    how Picks the sample slot A's Sample and Granular engines play, one of five built-in sounds or one you loaded.
    sound Choir and Strings are smooth and sustained, Bell and Pluck are short and decaying, and Texture is noisy and grainy.
ASmpRoot   "A root"        0 127  60   int 0                           | The note the sample sounds at its own pitch (MIDI note, 60 = C4)
    how Sets the MIDI note at which the sample plays at its own pitch, from 0 to 127 (60 is middle C).
    sound Setting it right makes the keyboard play in tune; moving it transposes the whole sample.
ASmpLoop   "A loop"        0 2    0    enum Off Forward Ping_pong      | Sample engine: how the sample loops while a note is held (Off: plays once)
    how Chooses how the Sample engine loops slot A's sample while a key is held: off, forward or back and forth.
    sound Off plays the sample once and then falls silent; looping holds the sound as long as the key is down.
ASmpLoopStart "A loop start" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop starts, as a share of the sample
    how Sets where the loop of slot A's sample begins, as a share of its length from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving it changes which part of the sample is repeated, so the held tone changes colour.
ASmpLoopEnd "A loop end"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop ends, as a share of the sample
    how Sets where the loop of slot A's sample ends, as a share of its length from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A shorter loop sounds more buzzy and pitched; a longer one keeps more of the sample's movement.
ASmpFade   "A loop fade"    0 1000 0    lin 0 500 ms 0                  | Sample engine: how long the loop's end fades into its start (0: a hard wrap, right for loops of whole periods; raise it when the loop points are not)
    how Sets how long the end of the loop fades into its start, from 0 to 500 ms.
    sound 0 ms is a hard wrap that suits loops of whole cycles; a longer fade hides the join but softens the sound.
ASmpRev    "A reverse"     0 1    0    switch                          | Sample engine: plays the sample backwards
    how Plays slot A's sample backwards when switched on.
    sound Reversed samples swell up into the note instead of striking, which sounds eerie and cinematic.
AGrSize    "A grain size"  0 1000 500  time 0.005 0.5                  | Granular engine: length of each grain
    how Sets the length of each grain in slot A's Granular engine, from 5 to 500 ms.
    sound Short grains sound buzzy and rough, long grains smooth and blurred; the longer they are, the more cost.
AGrRate    "A grain rate"  0 1000 700  freq 1 100                      | Granular engine: grains started per second (a little uneven, as grains in a cloud are)
    how Sets how many grains start each second in slot A, from 1 to 100.
    sound Low rates sound sparse and rhythmic, high rates form a dense continuous cloud.
AGrSpray   "A spray"       0 1000 100  pct                             | Granular engine: how far from the centre grains may start (100%: anywhere in the sample)
    how Sets how far from the centre position grains may start, from 0 to 100 % of the sample.
    sound At 0 % the sound is a stable, focused tone; more spray gives a diffuse, scattered cloud.
AGrScan    "A scan"        0 1000 500  lin -2 2 × 2                    | Granular engine: how fast the centre moves through the sample (1×: its own speed, 0: frozen, negative: backwards)
    how Sets how fast the grain centre moves through the sample, from 2 times backwards to 2 times forwards (1 is its own speed, 0 is frozen).
    sound At 0 the sound holds still like a frozen moment; other speeds sweep through the sample's evolution.
AGrJitter  "A grain pitch" 0 1000 0    pow 0 1200 2 ct 0               | Granular engine: how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note
    how Sets how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note, from 0 to 1200 cents.
    sound A little adds shimmer and width; a lot gives a detuned, chaotic, glittering cloud.
AGrShape   "A grain shape" 0 4    0    enum Hann Triangle Tukey Gauss Percussive | Granular engine: the window every grain fades in and out with
    how Chooses the fade-in and fade-out window each grain uses: Hann, Triangle, Tukey, Gauss or Percussive.
    sound Smooth windows blend grains into a pad; Percussive gives a clicky, rhythmic texture.
AGrRev     "A grain reverse" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Granular engine: the share of grains that play backwards
    how Sets the share of grains that play backwards, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More reversed grains add a sucking, washy, dreamlike quality.
AGrWidth   "A grain width" 0 1000 500  pct                             | Granular engine: how far grains scatter across the stereo field
    how Sets how far grains scatter across the stereo field, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher values make a wide, enveloping cloud; 0 % keeps it in the centre.
group Osc B
BSmpSrc    "B sample"      0 5    0    enum Choir Strings Bell Pluck Texture User | The sample the Sample and Granular engines play (built-in ones are made by code; User: one loaded for this slot)
    how Picks the sample slot B's Sample and Granular engines play, one of five built-in sounds or one you loaded.
    sound Choir and Strings are smooth and sustained, Bell and Pluck are short and decaying, and Texture is noisy and grainy.
BSmpRoot   "B root"        0 127  60   int 0                           | The note the sample sounds at its own pitch (MIDI note, 60 = C4)
    how Sets the MIDI note at which the sample plays at its own pitch, from 0 to 127 (60 is middle C).
    sound Setting it right makes the keyboard play in tune; moving it transposes the whole sample.
