    sound Low rates sound sparse and rhythmic, high rates form a dense continuous cloud.
BGrSpray   "B spray"       0 1000 100  pct                             | Granular engine: how far from the centre grains may start (100%: anywhere in the sample)
    how Sets how far from the centre position grains may start, from 0 to 100 % of the sample.
    sound At 0 % the sound is a stable, focused tone; more spray gives a diffuse, scattered cloud.
BGrScan    "B scan"        0 1000 500  lin -2 2 × 2                    | Granular engine: how fast the centre moves through the sample (1×: its own speed, 0: frozen, negative: backwards)
    how Sets how fast the grain centre moves through the sample, from 2 times backwards to 2 times forwards (1 is its own speed, 0 is frozen).
    sound At 0 the sound holds still like a frozen moment; other speeds sweep through the sample's evolution.
BGrJitter  "B grain pitch" 0 1000 0    pow 0 1200 2 ct 0               | Granular engine: how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note
    how Sets how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note, from 0 to 1200 cents.
    sound A little adds shimmer and width; a lot gives a detuned, chaotic, glittering cloud.
BGrShape   "B grain shape" 0 4    0    enum Hann Triangle Tukey Gauss Percussive | Granular engine: the window every grain fades in and out with
    how Chooses the fade-in and fade-out window each grain uses: Hann, Triangle, Tukey, Gauss or Percussive.
    sound Smooth windows blend grains into a pad; Percussive gives a clicky, rhythmic texture.
BGrRev     "B grain reverse" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Granular engine: the share of grains that play backwards
    how Sets the share of grains that play backwards, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More reversed grains add a sucking, washy, dreamlike quality.
BGrWidth   "B grain width" 0 1000 500  pct                             | Granular engine: how far grains scatter across the stereo field
    how Sets how far grains scatter across the stereo field, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher values make a wide, enveloping cloud; 0 % keeps it in the centre.
group Osc C
CSmpSrc    "C sample"      0 5    0    enum Choir Strings Bell Pluck Texture User | The sample the Sample and Granular engines play (built-in ones are made by code; User: one loaded for this slot)
    how Picks the sample slot C's Sample and Granular engines play, one of five built-in sounds or one you loaded.
    sound Choir and Strings are smooth and sustained, Bell and Pluck are short and decaying, and Texture is noisy and grainy.
CSmpRoot   "C root"        0 127  60   int 0                           | The note the sample sounds at its own pitch (MIDI note, 60 = C4)
    how Sets the MIDI note at which the sample plays at its own pitch, from 0 to 127 (60 is middle C).
    sound Setting it right makes the keyboard play in tune; moving it transposes the whole sample.
CSmpLoop   "C loop"        0 2    0    enum Off Forward Ping_pong      | Sample engine: how the sample loops while a note is held (Off: plays once)
    how Chooses how the Sample engine loops slot C's sample while a key is held: off, forward or back and forth.
    sound Off plays the sample once and then falls silent; looping holds the sound as long as the key is down.
CSmpLoopStart "C loop start" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop starts, as a share of the sample
    how Sets where the loop of slot C's sample begins, as a share of its length from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving it changes which part of the sample is repeated, so the held tone changes colour.
CSmpLoopEnd "C loop end"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop ends, as a share of the sample
    how Sets where the loop of slot C's sample ends, as a share of its length from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A shorter loop sounds more buzzy and pitched; a longer one keeps more of the sample's movement.
CSmpFade   "C loop fade"    0 1000 0    lin 0 500 ms 0                  | Sample engine: how long the loop's end fades into its start (0: a hard wrap, right for loops of whole periods; raise it when the loop points are not)
    how Sets how long the end of the loop fades into its start, from 0 to 500 ms.
    sound 0 ms is a hard wrap that suits loops of whole cycles; a longer fade hides the join but softens the sound.
CSmpRev    "C reverse"     0 1    0    switch                          | Sample engine: plays the sample backwards
    how Plays slot C's sample backwards when switched on.
    sound Reversed samples swell up into the note instead of striking, which sounds eerie and cinematic.
CGrSize    "C grain size"  0 1000 500  time 0.005 0.5                  | Granular engine: length of each grain
    how Sets the length of each grain in slot C's Granular engine, from 5 to 500 ms.
    sound Short grains sound buzzy and rough, long grains smooth and blurred; the longer they are, the more cost.
CGrRate    "C grain rate"  0 1000 700  freq 1 100                      | Granular engine: grains started per second (a little uneven, as grains in a cloud are)
    how Sets how many grains start each second in slot C, from 1 to 100.
    sound Low rates sound sparse and rhythmic, high rates form a dense continuous cloud.
CGrSpray   "C spray"       0 1000 100  pct                             | Granular engine: how far from the centre grains may start (100%: anywhere in the sample)
    how Sets how far from the centre position grains may start, from 0 to 100 % of the sample.
    sound At 0 % the sound is a stable, focused tone; more spray gives a diffuse, scattered cloud.
CGrScan    "C scan"        0 1000 500  lin -2 2 × 2                    | Granular engine: how fast the centre moves through the sample (1×: its own speed, 0: frozen, negative: backwards)
    how Sets how fast the grain centre moves through the sample, from 2 times backwards to 2 times forwards (1 is its own speed, 0 is frozen).
    sound At 0 the sound holds still like a frozen moment; other speeds sweep through the sample's evolution.
CGrJitter  "C grain pitch" 0 1000 0    pow 0 1200 2 ct 0               | Granular engine: how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note
    how Sets how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note, from 0 to 1200 cents.
    sound A little adds shimmer and width; a lot gives a detuned, chaotic, glittering cloud.
CGrShape   "C grain shape" 0 4    0    enum Hann Triangle Tukey Gauss Percussive | Granular engine: the window every grain fades in and out with
    how Chooses the fade-in and fade-out window each grain uses: Hann, Triangle, Tukey, Gauss or Percussive.
    sound Smooth windows blend grains into a pad; Percussive gives a clicky, rhythmic texture.
CGrRev     "C grain reverse" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Granular engine: the share of grains that play backwards
    how Sets the share of grains that play backwards, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More reversed grains add a sucking, washy, dreamlike quality.
CGrWidth   "C grain width" 0 1000 500  pct                             | Granular engine: how far grains scatter across the stereo field
    how Sets how far grains scatter across the stereo field, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher values make a wide, enveloping cloud; 0 % keeps it in the centre.

# P3a (appended): the Harmonic engine's parameters for each slot. "position" (above) morphs from the first set to the
# second; tuning, level, pan, unison, detune, spread and phase are the slot's own. Partials take no warps.
group Osc A
AHSet     "A harmonics"  0 13   0    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the first set of partial levels (made by code; User: the first frame of the slot's loaded wavetable, analysed)
    how Picks the first set of partial levels in slot A's Harmonic engine, such as Saw, Organ, Strings or a vowel.
    sound The set decides the basic tone colour, from bright and full to hollow, reedy or vocal.
AHSet2    "A harmonics 2" 0 13  1    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the second set, which "position" morphs to (User: the last frame of the slot's loaded wavetable)
    how Picks the second set of partial levels, which the position control morphs towards.
    sound Sweeping the position glides the tone from the first set to this one.
AHPartials "A partials"  1 128  32   int 0                           | Harmonic engine: how many partials sound (those above the Nyquist limit are dropped on high notes anyway); each added partial costs CPU
    how Sets how many sine partials sound in slot A, from 1 to 128.
    sound More partials sound fuller and brighter but cost CPU for each one; fewer sound plainer and mellower.
AHTilt    "A tilt"      0 1000 500  lin -24 24 dB/oct 1                 | Harmonic engine: brightness; each octave of partials louder (+) or softer (−) by this many dB on top of the set (loudness stays)
    how Tilts the brightness of the partials by up to 24 dB per octave either way, keeping the loudness.
    sound Positive values sound brighter and sharper, negative values darker and softer.
AHOddEven "A odd even"  0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: + weakens the even partials (towards a hollow, odd-only tone), − weakens the odd ones (towards the octave above)
    how Weakens the even partials (positive) or the odd ones (negative), from -100 to +100 %.
    sound Weaker even partials sound hollow like a clarinet; weaker odd ones sound thin, an octave higher.
AHStretch "A stretch"   0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: spreads the partials from whole multiples of the pitch: + stretches them apart (bells, glass, plucked wire), − bunches them (clusters)
    how Moves the partials away from whole multiples of the pitch, from -100 to +100 %.
    sound Stretching sounds like bells, glass or plucked wire; compressing bunches them into clusters.
AHDamp    "A damp"      0 1000 0    pct                             | Harmonic engine: how fast the upper partials die away while a note is held (0: they last; 100%: a pluck)
    how Sets how fast the upper partials die away while a note is held, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound At 0 % they last; at 100 % the sound dies away like a pluck.
group Osc B
BHSet     "B harmonics"  0 13   0    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the first set of partial levels (made by code; User: the first frame of the slot's loaded wavetable, analysed)
    how Picks the first set of partial levels in slot B's Harmonic engine, such as Saw, Organ, Strings or a vowel.
    sound The set decides the basic tone colour, from bright and full to hollow, reedy or vocal.
BHSet2    "B harmonics 2" 0 13  1    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the second set, which "position" morphs to (User: the last frame of the slot's loaded wavetable)
    how Picks the second set of partial levels, which the position control morphs towards.
    sound Sweeping the position glides the tone from the first set to this one.
BHPartials "B partials"  1 128  32   int 0                           | Harmonic engine: how many partials sound (those above the Nyquist limit are dropped on high notes anyway); each added partial costs CPU
    how Sets how many sine partials sound in slot B, from 1 to 128.
    sound More partials sound fuller and brighter but cost CPU for each one; fewer sound plainer and mellower.
BHTilt    "B tilt"      0 1000 500  lin -24 24 dB/oct 1                 | Harmonic engine: brightness; each octave of partials louder (+) or softer (−) by this many dB on top of the set (loudness stays)
    how Tilts the brightness of the partials by up to 24 dB per octave either way, keeping the loudness.
    sound Positive values sound brighter and sharper, negative values darker and softer.
BHOddEven "B odd even"  0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: + weakens the even partials (towards a hollow, odd-only tone), − weakens the odd ones (towards the octave above)
    how Weakens the even partials (positive) or the odd ones (negative), from -100 to +100 %.
    sound Weaker even partials sound hollow like a clarinet; weaker odd ones sound thin, an octave higher.
BHStretch "B stretch"   0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: spreads the partials from whole multiples of the pitch: + stretches them apart (bells, glass, plucked wire), − bunches them (clusters)
    how Moves the partials away from whole multiples of the pitch, from -100 to +100 %.
    sound Stretching sounds like bells, glass or plucked wire; compressing bunches them into clusters.
BHDamp    "B damp"      0 1000 0    pct                             | Harmonic engine: how fast the upper partials die away while a note is held (0: they last; 100%: a pluck)
    how Sets how fast the upper partials die away while a note is held, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound At 0 % they last; at 100 % the sound dies away like a pluck.
group Osc C
CHSet     "C harmonics"  0 13   0    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the first set of partial levels (made by code; User: the first frame of the slot's loaded wavetable, analysed)
    how Picks the first set of partial levels in slot C's Harmonic engine, such as Saw, Organ, Strings or a vowel.
    sound The set decides the basic tone colour, from bright and full to hollow, reedy or vocal.
CHSet2    "C harmonics 2" 0 13  1    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the second set, which "position" morphs to (User: the last frame of the slot's loaded wavetable)
    how Picks the second set of partial levels, which the position control morphs towards.
    sound Sweeping the position glides the tone from the first set to this one.
CHPartials "C partials"  1 128  32   int 0                           | Harmonic engine: how many partials sound (those above the Nyquist limit are dropped on high notes anyway); each added partial costs CPU
    how Sets how many sine partials sound in slot C, from 1 to 128.
    sound More partials sound fuller and brighter but cost CPU for each one; fewer sound plainer and mellower.
CHTilt    "C tilt"      0 1000 500  lin -24 24 dB/oct 1                 | Harmonic engine: brightness; each octave of partials louder (+) or softer (−) by this many dB on top of the set (loudness stays)
    how Tilts the brightness of the partials by up to 24 dB per octave either way, keeping the loudness.
    sound Positive values sound brighter and sharper, negative values darker and softer.
CHOddEven "C odd even"  0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: + weakens the even partials (towards a hollow, odd-only tone), − weakens the odd ones (towards the octave above)
    how Weakens the even partials (positive) or the odd ones (negative), from -100 to +100 %.
    sound Weaker even partials sound hollow like a clarinet; weaker odd ones sound thin, an octave higher.
CHStretch "C stretch"   0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: spreads the partials from whole multiples of the pitch: + stretches them apart (bells, glass, plucked wire), − bunches them (clusters)
    how Moves the partials away from whole multiples of the pitch, from -100 to +100 %.
    sound Stretching sounds like bells, glass or plucked wire; compressing bunches them into clusters.
CHDamp    "C damp"      0 1000 0    pct                             | Harmonic engine: how fast the upper partials die away while a note is held (0: they last; 100%: a pluck)
    how Sets how fast the upper partials die away while a note is held, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound At 0 % they last; at 100 % the sound dies away like a pluck.

# P3b (appended): the Modal engine's parameters for each slot: a bank of resonating modes (spacing by geometry, loss by material,
# ring time and body size) excited by a mallet, a pluck or a continuous bow/breath. "position" (above) is where on the body it is
# excited. Tuning, level, pan, unison, detune, spread and phase are the slot's own. Modes take no warps.
group Osc A
AMExc     "A exciter" 0 2 0 enum Struck Plucked Continuous | Modal engine: what excites the body: a mallet strike, a plucked release, or a continuous noise-driven bow or breath that sounds while the key is held
    how Chooses what excites the resonating body of slot A: a mallet strike, a pluck or a continuous bow or breath.
    sound Struck rings and fades, plucked sounds like a string, and continuous keeps sounding as long as the key is held.
AMForce   "A force" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: how hard it is excited: harder is brighter (a harder mallet, a sharper pluck, a pressed bow); loudness stays
    how Sets how hard the body of slot A is excited, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Harder sounds brighter, like a hard mallet or a pressed bow, at the same loudness.
AMGeom    "A geometry" 0 5 0 enum String Tube Bar Membrane Plate Bell | Modal engine: the body whose modes sound: a string (whole multiples), a tube closed at one end (odd multiples), a free bar, a drum membrane, a plate or a bell (the spacings of each, not whole multiples)
    how Chooses the shape of the body: string, tube, bar, membrane, plate or bell.
    sound A string sounds harmonic, a tube hollow, a bar and plate metallic, a membrane drum-like and a bell clangorous.
AMModes   "A modes" 1 64 24 int 0 | Modal engine: how many modes sound, lowest first (a membrane has 31, a bell 12; those above the Nyquist limit are dropped on high notes); each mode costs CPU
    how Sets how many resonating modes the body has, from 1 to 64, lowest first.
    sound More modes sound richer and more detailed and cost CPU for each one; fewer sound simpler and duller.
AMMat     "A material" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: soft to hard: 0 is gut, felt or skin (exact spacing, the upper modes die fast), 100% is glass or steel (stiffness stretches the spacing, the upper modes ring on)
    how Sets how hard the body's material is, from soft (0 %, like gut or felt) to hard (100 %, like glass or steel).
    sound Soft is warm and dies quickly; hard is bright, stiff and rings on.
AMRing    "A ring time" 0 1000 568 time 0.05 20 | Modal engine: how long the lowest mode takes to fall by 60 dB (the damping of the body)
    how Sets how long the lowest mode takes to fall by 60 dB, from 50 ms to 20 s.
    sound Short is a dry thud or click; long is a ringing, sustained tone.
AMHfDamp  "A hf damp" 0 1000 300 pct | Modal engine: how much faster the upper modes die than the lowest (the loss grows with the square of the frequency; the material softens or hardens it)
    how Sets how much faster the upper modes die than the lowest, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher values make a warm, mellow sound where the brightness fades quickly.
AMSize    "A body size" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: small to large body: a larger one rings longer and favours the low modes, a smaller one the high ones
    how Sets the size of the body from small to large, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A larger body rings longer and favours the lows; a smaller one is brighter and shorter.

group Osc B
BMExc     "B exciter" 0 2 0 enum Struck Plucked Continuous | Modal engine: what excites the body: a mallet strike, a plucked release, or a continuous noise-driven bow or breath that sounds while the key is held
    how Chooses what excites the resonating body of slot B: a mallet strike, a pluck or a continuous bow or breath.
    sound Struck rings and fades, plucked sounds like a string, and continuous keeps sounding as long as the key is held.
BMForce   "B force" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: how hard it is excited: harder is brighter (a harder mallet, a sharper pluck, a pressed bow); loudness stays
    how Sets how hard the body of slot B is excited, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Harder sounds brighter, like a hard mallet or a pressed bow, at the same loudness.
BMGeom    "B geometry" 0 5 0 enum String Tube Bar Membrane Plate Bell | Modal engine: the body whose modes sound: a string (whole multiples), a tube closed at one end (odd multiples), a free bar, a drum membrane, a plate or a bell (the spacings of each, not whole multiples)
    how Chooses the shape of the body: string, tube, bar, membrane, plate or bell.
    sound A string sounds harmonic, a tube hollow, a bar and plate metallic, a membrane drum-like and a bell clangorous.
BMModes   "B modes" 1 64 24 int 0 | Modal engine: how many modes sound, lowest first (a membrane has 31, a bell 12; those above the Nyquist limit are dropped on high notes); each mode costs CPU
    how Sets how many resonating modes the body has, from 1 to 64, lowest first.
    sound More modes sound richer and more detailed and cost CPU for each one; fewer sound simpler and duller.
BMMat     "B material" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: soft to hard: 0 is gut, felt or skin (exact spacing, the upper modes die fast), 100% is glass or steel (stiffness stretches the spacing, the upper modes ring on)
    how Sets how hard the body's material is, from soft (0 %, like gut or felt) to hard (100 %, like glass or steel).
    sound Soft is warm and dies quickly; hard is bright, stiff and rings on.
BMRing    "B ring time" 0 1000 568 time 0.05 20 | Modal engine: how long the lowest mode takes to fall by 60 dB (the damping of the body)
    how Sets how long the lowest mode takes to fall by 60 dB, from 50 ms to 20 s.
    sound Short is a dry thud or click; long is a ringing, sustained tone.
BMHfDamp  "B hf damp" 0 1000 300 pct | Modal engine: how much faster the upper modes die than the lowest (the loss grows with the square of the frequency; the material softens or hardens it)
    how Sets how much faster the upper modes die than the lowest, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher values make a warm, mellow sound where the brightness fades quickly.
BMSize    "B body size" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: small to large body: a larger one rings longer and favours the low modes, a smaller one the high ones
    how Sets the size of the body from small to large, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A larger body rings longer and favours the lows; a smaller one is brighter and shorter.

group Osc C
CMExc     "C exciter" 0 2 0 enum Struck Plucked Continuous | Modal engine: what excites the body: a mallet strike, a plucked release, or a continuous noise-driven bow or breath that sounds while the key is held
    how Chooses what excites the resonating body of slot C: a mallet strike, a pluck or a continuous bow or breath.
    sound Struck rings and fades, plucked sounds like a string, and continuous keeps sounding as long as the key is held.
CMForce   "C force" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: how hard it is excited: harder is brighter (a harder mallet, a sharper pluck, a pressed bow); loudness stays
    how Sets how hard the body of slot C is excited, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Harder sounds brighter, like a hard mallet or a pressed bow, at the same loudness.
CMGeom    "C geometry" 0 5 0 enum String Tube Bar Membrane Plate Bell | Modal engine: the body whose modes sound: a string (whole multiples), a tube closed at one end (odd multiples), a free bar, a drum membrane, a plate or a bell (the spacings of each, not whole multiples)
    how Chooses the shape of the body: string, tube, bar, membrane, plate or bell.
    sound A string sounds harmonic, a tube hollow, a bar and plate metallic, a membrane drum-like and a bell clangorous.
CMModes   "C modes" 1 64 24 int 0 | Modal engine: how many modes sound, lowest first (a membrane has 31, a bell 12; those above the Nyquist limit are dropped on high notes); each mode costs CPU
    how Sets how many resonating modes the body has, from 1 to 64, lowest first.
    sound More modes sound richer and more detailed and cost CPU for each one; fewer sound simpler and duller.
CMMat     "C material" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: soft to hard: 0 is gut, felt or skin (exact spacing, the upper modes die fast), 100% is glass or steel (stiffness stretches the spacing, the upper modes ring on)
    how Sets how hard the body's material is, from soft (0 %, like gut or felt) to hard (100 %, like glass or steel).
    sound Soft is warm and dies quickly; hard is bright, stiff and rings on.
CMRing    "C ring time" 0 1000 568 time 0.05 20 | Modal engine: how long the lowest mode takes to fall by 60 dB (the damping of the body)
    how Sets how long the lowest mode takes to fall by 60 dB, from 50 ms to 20 s.
    sound Short is a dry thud or click; long is a ringing, sustained tone.
CMHfDamp  "C hf damp" 0 1000 300 pct | Modal engine: how much faster the upper modes die than the lowest (the loss grows with the square of the frequency; the material softens or hardens it)
    how Sets how much faster the upper modes die than the lowest, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Higher values make a warm, mellow sound where the brightness fades quickly.
CMSize    "C body size" 0 1000 500 pct | Modal engine: small to large body: a larger one rings longer and favours the low modes, a smaller one the high ones
    how Sets the size of the body from small to large, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A larger body rings longer and favours the lows; a smaller one is brighter and shorter.

# P4a: the arpeggiator, the step sequencer (its steps are in the machine state) and live MPE.
group Arp
ArpMode    "Arp mode"      0 6    0    enum Off Up Down Up_Down Played Random Chord | Arpeggiator: how the held notes are played one by one on the song's grid (Off: the notes sound as played; Played: in the order they were pressed; Random: a seeded draw; Chord: all held notes at once, shifted up each step across the octave range). Overridden by the sequencer in Notes mode
    how Chooses how the arpeggiator plays held notes one at a time: up, down, up and down, as played, random or as a chord.
    sound Off passes notes through; the other modes turn held chords into a running pattern.
ArpRate    "Arp rate"      0 5    1    enum 1/32 1/16 1/8 1/4 1/2 1_bar | Arpeggiator: the length of a step (a quarter note is a beat)
    how Sets the arpeggiator step length, from a 32nd note to a whole bar.
    sound Short steps sound fast and busy, long ones slow and spacious.
ArpFeel    "Arp feel"      0 2    0    enum Straight Dotted Triplet | Arpeggiator: straight steps, dotted (1.5 x as long) or triplet (2/3 as long)
    how Chooses straight, dotted (1.5 times as long) or triplet (two thirds as long) arpeggiator steps.
    sound Triplets and dotted notes add a rolling or lilting feel.
ArpOct     "Arp octaves"   0 3    0    int 1 oct | Arpeggiator: how many octaves the held notes are repeated across (upwards)
    how Sets how many octaves the arpeggio repeats across, from 1 to 4.
    sound More octaves make a wider, rising pattern.
ArpGate    "Arp gate"      0 1000 600  pct | Arpeggiator: how much of its step each note sounds (5% at least)
    how Sets how much of each step a note sounds, from 5 to 100 %.
    sound Low sounds short and staccato, high sounds long and legato.
ArpSwing   "Arp swing"     0 1000 0    pct | Arpeggiator: delays every second step, by up to half a step at 100% (66% is a triplet feel)
    how Delays every second arpeggiator step by up to half a step.
    sound More swing sounds looser and groovier; 66 % is a triplet feel.
ArpLatch   "Arp latch"     0 1    0    switch | Arpeggiator: keep the notes going after the keys are released; the next key played replaces them
    how Keeps the arpeggio playing after the keys are released; the next key played replaces it.
    sound It frees your hands while the pattern keeps running.
ArpSeed    "Arp seed"      0 255  0    int 0 | Arpeggiator and sequencer: the seed of the random mode and of the step probabilities (the same seed gives the same notes in every render)
    how Sets the seed, from 0 to 255, of the random arpeggio and of the step probabilities.
    sound The same seed gives the same notes every time, so a render repeats exactly.

group Seq
SeqMode    "Seq mode"      0 2    0    enum Off Notes Mod | Step sequencer: Notes plays the steps on the held key (the arpeggiator stands aside), Mod only runs the steps as modulation sources (Seq step, Seq velocity). The steps are edited on the Arp page and kept in the song
    how Chooses what the step sequencer does: off, play the steps as notes on the held key, or only run them as modulation sources.
    sound Notes turns a held key into a melodic pattern; Mod moves other controls in steps.
SeqLength  "Seq length"    0 31   15   int 1 | Step sequencer: the number of steps (1 to 32)
    how Sets how many steps the sequencer plays, from 1 to 32.
    sound Short loops repeat quickly and feel tight; long ones evolve.
SeqRate    "Seq rate"      0 5    1    enum 1/32 1/16 1/8 1/4 1/2 1_bar | Step sequencer: the length of a step
    how Sets the sequencer step length, from a 32nd note to a whole bar.
    sound Short steps sound fast and busy, long ones slow and spacious.
SeqFeel    "Seq feel"      0 2    0    enum Straight Dotted Triplet | Step sequencer: straight steps, dotted or triplet
    how Chooses straight, dotted or triplet sequencer steps.
    sound Triplets and dotted notes add a rolling or lilting feel.
SeqSwing   "Seq swing"     0 1000 0    pct | Step sequencer: delays every second step, by up to half a step at 100%
    how Delays every second sequencer step by up to half a step.
    sound More swing sounds looser and groovier.
SeqSlew    "Seq slew"      0 1000 0    pct | Step sequencer: how smoothly the modulation sources glide from one step to the next (0: stepped, 100%: a whole step)
    how Sets how smoothly the sequencer's modulation sources glide from step to step, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound At 0 % the changes jump in steps; at 100 % they glide through the whole step.

group MPE
MpeMode    "MPE"           0 1    0    switch Off On | Live MPE: notes keep the MIDI channel they came on (channel 1 is the master): each member channel's pitch bend, pressure and slide (CC74) move that note alone, as the modulation sources MPE bend, MPE pressure and MPE slide. Off: channels are ignored
    how Switches live MPE on, so each note keeps its own MIDI channel and its own pitch bend, pressure and slide.
    sound Each finger can bend and shape its own note; off ignores the channels.
MpeBend    "MPE bend range" 0 96  48   int 0 st | Live MPE: the pitch bend range of a member channel, in semitones (48 is the MPE default)
    how Sets the pitch bend range of each MPE member channel, from 0 to 96 semitones.
    sound 48 is the usual MPE range; a smaller value makes each finger's pitch moves smaller.

# P4b0: the effects rack (docs/specs/dye-essence.md section 4.10): ten slots, each a type, a mix and ten generic parameters whose meaning the type gives (the engines of Neo EQ, Neo Filter, Neo Comp, Neo Clipper, Neo Delay and Neo Verb). Which chain a slot is in, and the order, are in the machine state (FxRouting).
group FX
FxLayout    "FX layout"     0 1    0    enum Trio Duo   | Trio: bus A and bus B (parallel sends from the synth) and a main chain (serial on the sum). Duo: insert 1 and insert 2 in series, then an aux (a send and return). Which slots sit in which chain: the machine state (default: slots 1-4 bus A or insert 1, 5-7 bus B or insert 2, 8-10 main or aux)
    how Chooses the rack's layout: Trio (two parallel buses and a main chain) or Duo (two inserts in series, then an aux).
    sound It decides whether effects work as parallel sends or as a serial chain.
FxSendA     "FX send A"     0 1000 870  db -40 6 inf   | Level sent to bus A (Trio) or to the aux (Duo)
    how Sets the level sent to bus A (Trio) or to the aux (Duo), from -40 dB to +6 dB.
    sound More send sounds wetter through the effects on that chain.
FxSendB     "FX send B"     0 1000 870  db -40 6 inf   | Level sent to bus B (Trio; unused in Duo)
    how Sets the level sent to bus B (Trio only), from -40 dB to +6 dB.
    sound More send sounds wetter through the effects on bus B; it does nothing in Duo.
FxRetA      "FX return A"   0 1000 870  db -40 6 inf   | Level of bus A (Trio) or of the aux (Duo) back into the mix
    how Sets the level of bus A (Trio) or the aux (Duo) returned to the mix, from -40 dB to +6 dB.
    sound It sets how loud the processed signal is next to the dry sound.
FxRetB      "FX return B"   0 1000 870  db -40 6 inf   | Level of bus B back into the mix (Trio; unused in Duo)
    how Sets the level of bus B returned to the mix (Trio only), from -40 dB to +6 dB.
    sound It sets how loud bus B is next to the dry sound; it does nothing in Duo.
X1Type "FX1 type" 0 12 0 enum Off EQ Filter Comp Clipper Delay Verb Dimension Bitcrusher Freq_shift Pitch_delay Convolution Vocoder | Effect slot 1: Off, or the engine of Neo EQ (four bands), Neo Filter, Neo Comp, Neo Clipper, Neo Delay or Neo Verb; or Dimension (a stereo-widening chorus), Bitcrusher (with wow and flutter), Freq shift (a frequency shifter) or Pitch delay (a delay with a pitch shifter in its feedback); Convolution (a partitioned convolution reverb of built-in or imported impulse responses) or Vocoder (a channel vocoder, its modulator an internal voice or an imported sample)
    how Chooses the effect in slot 1: off, EQ, filter, compressor, clipper, delay, reverb, dimension, bitcrusher, frequency shifter, pitch delay, convolution or vocoder.
    sound Each type has its own sound; it also decides what the ten p controls of the slot mean.
X1Mix  "FX1 mix" 0 1000 1000 pct | Effect slot 1: dry to wet (the dry signal is delayed to match the effect's latency). Set a delay or a reverb below 100 % in a serial chain
    how Sets how much of effect slot 1 is heard against the dry signal, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Keep delays and reverbs below 100 % in a serial chain to hear the dry sound as well.
X1P1 "FX1 p1" 0 1000 500 pct | Effect slot 1, parameter 1, as the type names it (0-100 % spans the engine parameter's range, 50 % is the engine's own default). EQ: Low freq; Filter: Type; Comp: Mode; Clipper: Drive; Delay: Mode; Verb: Mode; Dimension: Voices; Bitcrusher: Bits; Freq shift: Shift; Pitch delay: Time; Convolution: IR; Vocoder: Modulator
    how Sets the slot's control number 1 as a share of its range, whose meaning depends on the effect type: EQ Low freq, Filter Type, Comp Mode, and others.
    sound What you hear depends on the type; at 50 % it sits at the effect's own default, and the effects guide lists every type's controls.
X1P2 "FX1 p2" 0 1000 500 pct | Effect slot 1, parameter 2, as the type names it (0-100 % spans the engine parameter's range, 50 % is the engine's own default). EQ: Low gain; Filter: Slope; Comp: Threshold; Clipper: Ceiling; Delay: Sync; Verb: Pre-delay; Dimension: Rate; Bitcrusher: Rate; Freq shift: Range; Pitch delay: Pitch; Convolution: Size; Vocoder: Bands
    how Sets the slot's control number 2 as a share of its range, whose meaning depends on the effect type: EQ Low gain, Filter Slope, Comp Threshold, and others.
    sound What you hear depends on the type; at 50 % it sits at the effect's own default, and the effects guide lists every type's controls.
X1P3 "FX1 p3" 0 1000 500 pct | Effect slot 1, parameter 3, as the type names it (0-100 % spans the engine parameter's range, 50 % is the engine's own default). EQ: Mid 1 freq; Filter: Cutoff; Comp: Ratio; Clipper: Shape; Delay: Feel; Verb: Size; Dimension: Depth; Bitcrusher: Anti-alias; Freq shift: Mode; Pitch delay: Fine; Convolution: Pre-delay; Vocoder: Formant
